<title>DUBAI: Saudi Arabian to start flights to South Africa.</title>
<headline>Saudi Arabian to start flights to South Africa.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>National carrier Saudi Arabian Airlines Corp said it would start twice-weekly scheduled services to South Africa, via Nairobi, on October 28.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-Nairobi-Johannesburg flights on Boeing 747 aircraft would be operated on Mondays and Saturdays, it said in a statement on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Monday flights will be on 747-300 aircraft and the Saturday flights will be on 747-100s.</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714-626990</p>
</text>
